        div.mt-6.space-y-6
          p Jon Ong is a Singaporean composer and multi-instrumentalist with over 13 years of experience in film, TV, and commercials. He composed the score for <em>The Accidental Getaway Driver</em>, directed by Sing J. Lee, who won the 2023 Sundance U.S. Dramatic Award for Best Director. The film had its theatrical release in 2025. Jon also scored <em>Border Hopper</em>, a 2024 Sundance selection directed by Nico Casavecchia.
          p Jon's extensive film credits include additional music for the two-time BAFTA-nominated <em>Paddington</em>, <em>The Family Plan 2</em> starring Mark Wahlberg and Michelle Monaghan, <em>Love The Coopers</em> starring Diane Keaton and Timothée Chalamet, <em>Whiskey Tango Foxtrot</em> and the Cinema Eye Honors-nominated <em>17 Blocks</em>.
          p In TV, Jon has contributed additional music to <em>The Dinosaurs</em>, <em>The Wheel of Time</em>, <em>Life on Our Planet</em>, <em>Dopesick</em>, <em>Joe vs. Carole</em>, and <em>His Dark Materials</em>. His versatility extends to national commercials, including scoring McDonald's <em>The Hamburglar</em>.
          p Beyond film and TV scoring, Jon has composed music for <em>Chase Champion</em>, a Nickelodeon web series, written additional music for <em>Dragon Age: The Veilguard</em>, a video game, served as the conductor for the <em>Game Awards</em> (2021), and was an orchestrator for <em>Arthur Newman</em> and for Amazon's <em>The Dangerous Book for Boys</em>.
          p Originally from Singapore and now based in Los Angeles, Jon began his music career as a guitarist before studying film scoring at Berklee College of Music. He has since worked alongside renowned composers Lorne Balfe, Nick Urata, and William Ross in his rise through the film scoring world in Los Angeles.
